in the networking stack.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:19.830
So instead of data moving
through the TCP/IP layers,

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:22.500
it's transferred directly
between application memory

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.900
and the network
interface, and the impact

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:27.000
of that is significantly
lower latency

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.090
and dramatically
reduced CPU overhead.

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.670
