00:38:35.880 --> 00:38:38.190
to sit in the VM
memory and clear text.

00:38:38.190 --> 00:38:41.370
With AI HSM, crypto
operations are offloaded

00:38:41.370 --> 00:38:46.230
to a local PCIE SRIOV
device on the node.

00:38:46.230 --> 00:38:49.820
Thus, enabling the keys to
remain inside the HSM boundary

00:38:49.820 --> 00:38:51.920
and the VM uses a
local interface

00:38:51.920 --> 00:38:54.410
to access them securely,
as shown in the diagram.

00:38:54.410 --> 00:38:57.410
This reduces exposure to
memory based attacks,

00:38:57.410 --> 00:38:59.030
while also improving
performance,

00:38:59.030 --> 00:39:02.370
combat with repeated
remote HSM calls.

00:39:02.370 --> 00:39:04.950
Now, practically this
changes the threat model.

00:39:04.950 --> 00:39:07.080
For example, even in
cases, like, crash dumps

00:39:07.080 --> 00:39:10.410
or memory inspection, sensitive
